    "background_story": "Amara was a skilled pastry chef who had always been fascinated by the art of confectionery. Growing up in a small town in Israel, she was particularly fond of the traditional Jaffa orange, known for its sweetness and juiciness. Inspired by its flavor, Amara created a signature dessert - a Jaffa orange cake with a hint of citrus and a crunchy orange blossom water glaze. The cake quickly became a sensation in local bakeries and cafes, earning Amara the nickname 'The Jaffa Queen.' As her fame grew, so did her passion for innovation, and she began experimenting with new Jaffa-inspired recipes. Amara's love for the Jaffa orange had not only brought her success but also connected her to her roots and the rich culinary heritage of her homeland.",
